{
 "turns": [
  {
   "idx": 0,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good afternoon, can I have you confirm your full name and date of birth?",
   "start": 0.05,
   "end": 3.99
  },
  {
   "idx": 1,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Guadalupe Rios. June 17th, 1965.",
   "start": 5.3,
   "end": 11.04
  },
  {
   "idx": 2,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Thank you, Mrs. Rios. Finally cooling off out there, huh?",
   "start": 12.32,
   "end": 15.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 3,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Thank God. I can walk in the evenings again without melting.",
   "start": 15.93,
   "end": 20.96
  },
  {
   "idx": 4,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's good to hear, actually, because we're here to talk about your diabetes. You're a 1c from last week came back at 8 .4%. In April it was 7.",
   "start": 21.58,
   "end": 30.58
  },
  {
   "idx": 5,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "6. I, I figured it went up. I have to tell you something. I stopped the glipizide.",
   "start": 31.02,
   "end": 39.16
  },
  {
   "idx": 6,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Okay, thanks for telling me. When did you stop it and what happened?",
   "start": 39.96,
   "end": 43.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 7,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "About two months ago, I was getting shaky and sweaty in the afternoons. One time, my sugar was 62, and I almost had to pull the car over.",
   "start": 44.53,
   "end": 58.18
  },
  {
   "idx": 8,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "That's scary and that was the right instinct. That was the 5 milligrams once a day.",
   "start": 58.8,
   "end": 62.98
  },
  {
   "idx": 9,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, the 5 in the morning. Since I stopped it, no more lows.",
   "start": 63.88,
   "end": 68.94
  },
  {
   "idx": 10,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "And the Metformin, you're still taking that.",
   "start": 69.88,
   "end": 71.66
  },
  {
   "idx": 11,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, 1 ,000 milligrams twice a day, with breakfast and dinner. My stomach is fine with it now. No.",
   "start": 72.34,
   "end": 81.82
  },
  {
   "idx": 12,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Good. What are your fasting sugars running at home?",
   "start": 82.56,
   "end": 84.64
  },
  {
   "idx": 13,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Mostly 150 to 180 in the morning.",
   "start": 86.26,
   "end": 90.74
  },
  {
   "idx": 14,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Are you more thirsty than usual or getting up at night to pee?",
   "start": 91.7,
   "end": 94.56
  },
  {
   "idx": 15,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Maybe a little more thirsty. Not up at night, no.",
   "start": 95.82,
   "end": 99.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 16,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any numbness or tingling in your feet?",
   "start": 100.62,
   "end": 102.24
  },
  {
   "idx": 17,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No.",
   "start": 103.06,
   "end": 103.42
  },
  {
   "idx": 18,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Any blurry vision and when was your last eye exam?",
   "start": 104.28,
   "end": 106.78
  },
  {
   "idx": 19,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "My eyes are fine. The eye exam, um, I think it was before COVID. I know it's been a while.",
   "start": 107.56,
   "end": 116.84
  },
  {
   "idx": 20,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "We'll take care of that today and remind me you're allergic to sulfa.",
   "start": 117.54,
   "end": 121.2
  },
  {
   "idx": 21,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Yes, the bactrim. I broke out in a rash all over my body.",
   "start": 122.12,
   "end": 127.3
  },
  {
   "idx": 22,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Got it that's still in your chart. How's the family?",
   "start": 127.84,
   "end": 129.82
  },
  {
   "idx": 23,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Good. My husband's sugar is worse than mine. They put him on insulin last month. So now we're both checking. It's like a competition. Well, I hope you're winning.",
   "start": 130.89,
   "end": 144.35
  },
  {
   "idx": 24,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Let me look at you. Blood pressure is 128 over 76, pulse 80, weight 186 pounds, about the same as April.",
   "start": 144.71,
   "end": 152.79
  },
  {
   "idx": 25,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Let me check your feet,",
   "start": 154.14,
   "end": 155.1
  },
  {
   "idx": 26,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "skin looks good, no sores or calluses. Pulses are strong in both feet and you can feel the monofilament everywhere I touched. Heart and lungs sound normal.",
   "start": 155.46,
   "end": 164.52
  },
  {
   "idx": 27,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Your other labs look good too,",
   "start": 166.07,
   "end": 167.61
  },
  {
   "idx": 28,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "kidney function is normal, the filtration rate is 78 and there's no protein in your urine",
   "start": 167.97,
   "end": 173.23
  },
  {
   "idx": 29,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "okay that's good news at least it is so to put it",
   "start": 173.84,
   "end": 178.5
  },
  {
   "idx": 30,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "together your type 2 diabetes is above our goal and the glipizide was causing low sugar so we'll leave that off for good keep the metformin 1000 milligrams twice a day i'd like to add a new medicine called impagloflozin 10 milligrams once a day in the morning it doesn't usually cause lows and it also protects the heart and",
   "start": 178.5,
   "end": 194.38
  },
  {
   "idx": 31,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "kidneys is it a shot no it's a pill",
   "start": 194.38,
   "end": 198.72
  },
  {
   "idx": 32,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "it works by letting you You pass extra sugar in the urine, so drink plenty of water and keep that area clean. If you get any itching or a yeast infection, call us, it's treatable. If you can't eat or drink because you're sick, skip it that day.",
   "start": 198.72,
   "end": 211.92
  },
  {
   "idx": 33,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Okay, water, I can do.",
   "start": 213.14,
   "end": 215.08
  },
  {
   "idx": 34,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "I'm also putting in a referral for a diabetic eye exam and keep up the evening walks, they really do help. We'll repeat the A1C in three months and see you then.",
   "start": 215.78,
   "end": 224.96
  },
  {
   "idx": 35,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "Can you send the eye doctor info to the portal? My daughter, Mary Eisler, reads it for me.",
   "start": 226.46,
   "end": 233.94
  },
  {
   "idx": 36,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Sure, is the portal email still LupeRio65 at example .com?",
   "start": 234.36,
   "end": 238.76
  },
  {
   "idx": 37,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "That's the one.",
   "start": 239.7,
   "end": 240.22
  },
  {
   "idx": 38,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "Great, and the Impaglaflauzin goes to your usual pharmacy. Any questions?",
   "start": 241.57,
   "end": 245.23
  },
  {
   "idx": 39,
   "speaker": "patient",
   "text": "No, I think I've got it. Thank you, doctor.",
   "start": 246.27,
   "end": 249.54
  },
  {
   "idx": 40,
   "speaker": "clinician",
   "text": "You're welcome. Enjoy those walks.",
   "start": 250.24,
   "end": 251.68
  }
 ],
